WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.939
A living crust is powerful precisely because it grows and

2
00:00:03.039 --> 00:00:05.498
spreads on its own. But that is also the danger,

3
00:00:05.598 --> 00:00:07.684
it must never spread where it should not.

4
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:12.583
Drop the bacteria in one spot. They multiply and diffuse outward

5
00:00:12.683 --> 00:00:15.895
across the sand, like a drop of ink spreading through water.

6
00:00:17.961 --> 00:00:22.327
So we engineer a kill switch. Cross an environmental line, leave the target

7
00:00:22.427 --> 00:00:25.959
zone, and a toxin gene switches on and shuts the colony down.

8
00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:31.273
So two forces are always in balance: growth that builds the crust, and

9
00:00:31.373 --> 00:00:35.163
containment that keeps it exactly where we want it, and nowhere else.

